  "description": "The language algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines: number conversion (Number::toString at every radix, toFixed, toExponential, toPrecision, StringToNumber, parseInt, parseFloat, numeric literal values, numeric keys and the string white-space set), numerics (the integer conversions, Float16, the Math kernels, exact rounding and the BigInt kernel) and text (UTF-16, padding and relative indices, replacement templates, the URI, base64 and hex codecs, and JSON's grammar, quoting and gap) and Date (the time-value arithmetic, the ISO calendar's civil-day helpers, the local-time provider with LocalTime and UTC, Date.parse's grammar in a strict and a Broiler.VM dialect, and the Date renderings) and time zones and calendar years (the decoder of the time-zone and calendar tables an engine hands in, lookup and primary identifiers, offsets and transitions with no 2037 cliff, possible instants, disambiguation, the start of a day, the offset time zones, and the Chinese, Korean, Umm al-Qura and Persian years), with the WorkCharge metering delegate, the ResultStatus enumeration and the limit records every shared operation uses.",
